{"issues":[{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"10139","self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/latest/issue/10139","key":"AP-22","fields":{"summary":"Implement extraction of history of changes ","issuetype":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issuetype/10037","id":"10037","description":"Stories track functionality or features expressed as user goals.","iconUrl":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10315?size=medium","name":"Story","subtask":false,"avatarId":10315,"entityId":"a9502e0d-867b-4e13-9c45-261e65fe910f","hierarchyLevel":0},"parent":{"id":"10033","key":"AP-1","self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/10033","fields":{"summary":"Core Scheduling Engine MVP","status":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/status/10066","description":"","iconUrl":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/","name":"To Do","id":"10066","statusCategory":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/statuscategory/2","id":2,"key":"new","colorName":"blue-gray","name":"To Do"}},"priority":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/priority/1","iconUrl":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/images/icons/priorities/highest_new.svg","name":"Highest","id":"1"},"issuetype":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issuetype/10035","id":"10035","description":"Epics track collections of related bugs, stories, and tasks.","iconUrl":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10307?size=medium","name":"Epic","subtask":false,"avatarId":10307,"entityId":"21b28705-2e2b-43f3-95af-c2d445b6d5a2","hierarchyLevel":1}}},"creator":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/user?accountId=712020%3Aef0c8c11-3cf2-4fc0-97ac-2cdbf24d876c","accountId":"712020:ef0c8c11-3cf2-4fc0-97ac-2cdbf24d876c","avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d94c6869cf0cb2ecec022ada4bff7684?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Fdefault-avatar-2.png","24x24":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d94c6869cf0cb2ecec022ada4bff7684?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Fdefault-avatar-2.png","16x16":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d94c6869cf0cb2ecec022ada4bff7684?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Fdefault-avatar-2.png","32x32":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d94c6869cf0cb2ecec022ada4bff7684?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Fdefault-avatar-2.png"},"displayName":"KidBlend App ","active":true,"timeZone":"Europe/Minsk","accountType":"atlassian"},"components":[],"created":"2025-12-16T23:46:20.083+0300","description":"# Solution Design: Change History Extraction Integration\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\n**Purpose**: This solution design documents the integration of change history extraction functionality into the existing `ingest-csv` command workflow. The feature enables project managers to extract and analyze historical changes for Status, Sprint, and Story Points fields from Jira tickets, supporting data-driven scheduling decisions.\r\n\r\n**Usage**: This design provides the technical architecture and implementation approach for adding change history extraction as an integrated step within the CSV ingestion pipeline.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Business Context\r\n\r\n### Problem Statement\r\n\r\nProject managers need to analyze historical changes to ticket fields (Status, Sprint, Story Points) to understand project evolution and make informed scheduling decisions. Currently, there is no automated way to extract and export this change history data from Jira tickets for analysis.\r\n\r\n### Business Objectives\r\n\r\n**Objective 1**: Enable automated extraction of change history for critical ticket fields (Status, Sprint, Story Points) to support historical analysis\r\n\r\n**Objective 2**: Integrate change history extraction seamlessly into the existing CSV ingestion workflow without disrupting current functionality\r\n\r\n**Objective 3**: Provide structured CSV output with complete change history data for downstream analysis and reporting\r\n\r\n### Success Criteria\r\n\r\n**Criterion 1**: Change history extraction runs automatically as part of `ingest-csv` command execution\r\n\r\n**Criterion 2**: All historical changes for Status, Sprint, and Story Points are extracted for tickets matching the configured JQL query\r\n\r\n**Criterion 3**: CSV output is generated in timestamped folders with proper formatting (ISO 8601 timestamps, display names, complete field information)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Solution Architecture\r\n\r\n### High-Level Architecture\r\n\r\n```mermaid\r\ngraph TB\r\n    subgraph \"Input Layer\"\r\n        A[CSV File Input]\r\n        B[Configuration File]\r\n        C[JQL Query Config]\r\n    end\r\n    subgraph \"Processing Layer\"\r\n        D[CSV Parser]\r\n        E[Change History Extractor]\r\n        F[Schedule Calculator]\r\n        G[Data Transformer]\r\n    end\r\n    subgraph \"Output Layer\"\r\n        H[output.json]\r\n        I[changes_history.csv]\r\n    end\r\n    A --> D\r\n    B --> D\r\n    C --> E\r\n    D --> F\r\n    E --> G\r\n    F --> H\r\n    G --> I\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Description**: The architecture extends the existing `ingest-csv` workflow by adding a parallel change history extraction process. The CSV parser and schedule calculator continue to operate as before, while the change history extractor processes tickets based on JQL configuration and generates a separate CSV output. Both processes run within the same command execution, sharing configuration context.\r\n\r\n### Component Architecture\r\n\r\n```mermaid\r\nflowchart TD\r\n    Start([ingest-csv Command]) --> ParseCSV[Parse CSV File]\r\n    ParseCSV --> ValidateCSV{Validate CSV Data}\r\n    ValidateCSV -->|Valid| InitConfig[Initialize Configuration]\r\n    ValidateCSV -->|Invalid| Error[Handle Error]\r\n    InitConfig --> ExtractHistory[Extract Change History]\r\n    InitConfig --> CalculateSchedule[Calculate Schedule]\r\n    ExtractHistory --> QueryTickets[Query Tickets via JQL]\r\n    QueryTickets --> GetChangelog[Get Changelog for Each Ticket]\r\n    GetChangelog --> FilterFields[Filter Status/Sprint/Story Points]\r\n    FilterFields --> TransformData[Transform to CSV Format]\r\n    TransformData --> CreateOutputDir[Create Timestamped Output Directory]\r\n    CreateOutputDir --> WriteCSV[Write changes_history.csv]\r\n    CalculateSchedule --> WriteJSON[Write output.json]\r\n    WriteCSV --> End([End])\r\n    WriteJSON --> End\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Description**: The workflow shows the parallel execution of schedule calculation and change history extraction. After configuration initialization, both processes proceed independently. The change history extraction follows a sequence: JQL query execution, changelog retrieval for each ticket, field filtering, data transformation, and CSV file generation in a timestamped directory.\r\n\r\n### Data Architecture\r\n\r\n```mermaid\r\nerDiagram\r\n    CONFIGURATION ||--o{ JQL_QUERY : contains\r\n    CONFIGURATION ||--o{ FIELD_MAPPING : defines\r\n    JQL_QUERY ||--o{ TICKET : matches\r\n    TICKET ||--o{ CHANGELOG_ENTRY : has\r\n    CHANGELOG_ENTRY ||--o{ FIELD_CHANGE : contains\r\n    FIELD_CHANGE ||--|| FIELD : references\r\n    FIELD_CHANGE ||--|| USER : changed_by\r\n    FIELD_CHANGE ||--|| TIMESTAMP : occurred_at\r\n    CSV_OUTPUT ||--o{ CSV_ROW : contains\r\n    CSV_ROW ||--|| TICKET : references\r\n    CSV_ROW ||--|| FIELD_CHANGE : represents\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Description**: The data model shows the relationships between configuration, tickets, changelog entries, and CSV output. Configuration defines JQL queries and field mappings. Tickets are matched by JQL queries and contain changelog entries. Each changelog entry contains field changes with references to the field, user who made the change, and timestamp. CSV output is composed of rows representing individual field changes.\r\n\r\n### Integration Architecture\r\n\r\n```mermaid\r\nsequenceDiagram\r\n    participant CLI as CLI Command\r\n    participant Parser as CSV Parser\r\n    participant Config as Config Manager\r\n    participant Extractor as Change History Extractor\r\n    participant JiraAPI as Jira API/dmtools\r\n    participant Transformer as Data Transformer\r\n    participant FileSystem as File System\r\n    participant Calculator as Schedule Calculator\r\n    \r\n    CLI->>Parser: Execute ingest-csv\r\n    CLI->>Config: Load Configuration\r\n    Parser->>Parser: Parse CSV File\r\n    Config->>Extractor: Provide JQL Query\r\n    Extractor->>JiraAPI: Execute JQL Query\r\n    JiraAPI-->>Extractor: Return Ticket Keys\r\n    Extractor->>JiraAPI: Get Changelog (per ticket)\r\n    JiraAPI-->>Extractor: Return Changelog Data\r\n    Extractor->>Transformer: Transform to CSV Format\r\n    Transformer->>FileSystem: Create Timestamped Directory\r\n    Transformer->>FileSystem: Write changes_history.csv\r\n    Parser->>Calculator: Calculate Schedule\r\n    Calculator->>FileSystem: Write output.json\r\n    FileSystem-->>CLI: Complete\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Description**: The sequence diagram illustrates the integration flow. The CLI command initiates both CSV parsing and change history extraction. Configuration is loaded once and shared. The extractor queries Jira via dmtools/Jira API, retrieves changelog data for each ticket, transforms it, and writes to a timestamped CSV file. The schedule calculation proceeds in parallel and writes its output separately.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Technical Design\r\n\r\n### Technology Stack\r\n\r\n**Runtime & Language:**\r\n- Node.js - Runtime environment for CLI execution\r\n- TypeScript - Type-safe implementation language\r\n\r\n**Libraries & Frameworks:**\r\n- Existing CSV parser - For CSV file processing\r\n- dmtools CLI - For Jira API interactions (changelog extraction)\r\n- fs (Node.js) - For file system operations (directory creation, file writing)\r\n- path (Node.js) - For path manipulation and timestamp-based directory naming\r\n\r\n**Tools & Infrastructure:**\r\n- Jira REST API - Alternative to dmtools if changelog command not available (via expand=changelog parameter)\r\n- Existing configuration system - For JQL query and field mapping configuration\r\n\r\n### Design Patterns\r\n\r\n**Pattern 1: Command Integration Pattern** - The change history extraction is integrated as an additional step within the existing `ingest-csv` command, maintaining backward compatibility while extending functionality.\r\n\r\n**Pattern 2: Parallel Processing Pattern** - Schedule calculation and change history extraction run in parallel after shared configuration initialization, optimizing execution time.\r\n\r\n**Pattern 3: Data Transformation Pattern** - Raw changelog data from Jira API is transformed into a normalized CSV format with consistent field names, timestamps, and user display names.\r\n\r\n### Security Considerations\r\n\r\n**Security measure 1**: Jira API credentials are managed through existing dmtools configuration (environment variables), not hardcoded in the application.\r\n\r\n**Security measure 2**: File system operations use safe path construction to prevent directory traversal vulnerabilities when creating timestamped output directories.\r\n\r\n**Security measure 3**: JQL query validation ensures only read operations are performed, preventing accidental data modification.\r\n\r\n### Performance Considerations\r\n\r\n**Performance optimization 1**: Batch processing of tickets - process multiple tickets concurrently when retrieving changelog data to reduce total API call time.\r\n\r\n**Performance optimization 2**: Caching of field mappings - store custom field codes (Sprint, Story Points) in memory after initial lookup to avoid repeated API calls.\r\n\r\n**Performance optimization 3**: Lazy directory creation - only create the timestamped output directory when change history data is successfully retrieved.\r\n\r\n### Scalability Considerations\r\n\r\n**Scalability approach 1**: Pagination support for JQL queries - handle large result sets by implementing pagination when querying tickets via JQL.\r\n\r\n**Scalability approach 2**: Rate limiting awareness - respect Jira API rate limits by implementing appropriate delays between API calls when processing large numbers of tickets.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Development Scope Decomposition\r\n\r\n### Decomposition Strategy\r\n\r\n**Important**: This solution is designed as a single implementation scope. The change history extraction feature is tightly integrated with the existing `ingest-csv` command and shares configuration and execution context. Decomposition into separate components would create unnecessary overhead and artificial boundaries.\r\n\r\n**Approach: Single Solution Design**\r\n\r\nThe scope is manageable as a single implementation unit because:\r\n- The feature extends an existing command with a clear integration point\r\n- Configuration and data flow are straightforward\r\n- All components (JQL query, changelog extraction, CSV generation) work together as a cohesive unit\r\n- No clear technical boundaries exist that would benefit from separation\r\n\r\n### Component: Change History Extraction Integration\r\n\r\n**Scope**: Integration of change history extraction into the `ingest-csv` command, including JQL-based ticket querying, changelog retrieval, field filtering, data transformation, and CSV file generation.\r\n\r\n**Task 1.1: Configuration Extension**\r\n\r\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\r\n- * AC1: Configuration file supports optional `changeHistory` section with `jql` property for ticket scope definition\r\n- * AC2: Configuration supports optional field mapping for Sprint and Story Points custom field codes\r\n- * AC3: Configuration validation handles missing or invalid JQL queries gracefully\r\n\r\n**Dependencies**: None (extends existing configuration system)\r\n\r\n**Estimated Effort**: 2 story points\r\n\r\n**Task 1.2: JQL Query Execution and Ticket Retrieval**\r\n\r\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\r\n- * AC1: System executes JQL query from configuration to retrieve matching ticket keys\r\n- * AC2: System handles pagination for JQL queries returning large result sets\r\n- * AC3: System logs the number of tickets found for change history extraction\r\n\r\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.1 (Configuration Extension)\r\n\r\n**Estimated Effort**: 3 story points\r\n\r\n**Task 1.3: Changelog Data Extraction**\r\n\r\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\r\n- * AC1: System retrieves complete changelog for each ticket using dmtools command or Jira REST API\r\n- * AC2: System extracts all historical changes (from ticket creation to present) for Status, Sprint, and Story Points fields\r\n- * AC3: System handles tickets with no changelog data gracefully (skips or logs warning)\r\n- * AC4: System uses field mapping configuration to correctly identify Sprint and Story Points custom fields\r\n\r\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.2 (JQL Query Execution)\r\n\r\n**Estimated Effort**: 5 story points\r\n\r\n**Task 1.4: Data Transformation and CSV Generation**\r\n\r\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\r\n- * AC1: System transforms changelog data into CSV rows with columns: Issue key, Field name, Value, Changed at (ISO 8601), Changed by (display name)\r\n- * AC2: System creates timestamped output directory in format `./output/YYYYMMDD_HH/`\r\n- * AC3: System writes CSV file with header row to `./output/YYYYMMDD_HH/changes_history.csv`\r\n- * AC4: System handles file system errors (permissions, disk space) with appropriate error messages\r\n- * AC5: All timestamps are formatted in ISO 8601 format\r\n- * AC6: User information displays as display names (not account IDs)\r\n\r\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.3 (Changelog Data Extraction)\r\n\r\n**Estimated Effort**: 3 story points\r\n\r\n**Task 1.5: Integration with ingest-csv Command**\r\n\r\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\r\n- * AC1: Change history extraction runs automatically when `ingest-csv` command is executed\r\n- * AC2: Change history extraction does not break existing `ingest-csv` functionality (CSV parsing and schedule calculation)\r\n- * AC3: System handles errors in change history extraction without failing the entire command (logs error, continues with schedule calculation)\r\n- * AC4: System provides appropriate logging for change history extraction progress and completion\r\n\r\n**Dependencies**: Task 1.4 (Data Transformation and CSV Generation)\r\n\r\n**Estimated Effort**: 2 story points\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Development Workflow\r\n\r\n```mermaid\r\ngraph LR\r\n    A[Planning] --> B[Design]\r\n    B --> C[Development]\r\n    C --> D[Code Review]\r\n    D --> E[Testing]\r\n    E --> F{Pass?}\r\n    F -->|Yes| G[Deploy]\r\n    F -->|No| C\r\n    G --> H[Monitor]\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Description**: Standard development workflow applies. Development includes unit tests for each component (configuration, JQL query, changelog extraction, CSV generation), integration tests for the complete workflow, and manual testing with real Jira data. Code review ensures adherence to existing code style and architecture patterns.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Dependencies & Risks\r\n\r\n### Dependencies\r\n\r\n**External Dependency 1**: dmtools changelog extraction command availability - If the command doesn't exist, implementation must use Jira REST API directly with `expand=changelog` parameter. **Impact if delayed**: Requires additional implementation work for REST API integration.\r\n\r\n**External Dependency 2**: Jira API access and permissions - The system requires read access to ticket changelogs via Jira API. **Impact if delayed**: Feature cannot function without proper API access.\r\n\r\n**Internal Dependency 1**: Existing configuration system - Change history configuration must integrate with current configuration loading and validation. **Impact if delayed**: Configuration extension work may need to be completed first.\r\n\r\n### Risks & Mitigation\r\n\r\n**Risk 1**: Large number of tickets causing performance issues or API rate limiting\r\n\r\n**Probability**: Medium\r\n\r\n**Impact**: High\r\n\r\n**Mitigation**: Implement pagination for JQL queries, batch processing with rate limiting, and progress logging. Consider implementing a limit on the number of tickets processed in a single run.\r\n\r\n**Risk 2**: Custom field codes for Sprint and Story Points may vary across Jira instances\r\n\r\n**Probability**: Medium\r\n\r\n**Impact**: Medium\r\n\r\n**Mitigation**: Use commonly used field codes as defaults, provide configuration option to override, and implement field code lookup using `dmtools jira_get_field_custom_code` command if needed.\r\n\r\n**Risk 3**: Changelog data structure may vary or be incomplete for some tickets\r\n\r\n**Probability**: Low\r\n\r\n**Impact**: Medium\r\n\r\n**Mitigation**: Implement robust error handling for missing or malformed changelog data, log warnings for skipped records, and validate data structure before transformation.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Testing Strategy\r\n\r\n### Unit Testing\r\n\r\n**Coverage target**: 80% minimum\r\n\r\n**Key areas**: \r\n- Configuration parsing and validation\r\n- JQL query execution and pagination\r\n- Changelog data parsing and field filtering\r\n- CSV data transformation and formatting\r\n- Timestamp formatting (ISO 8601)\r\n- Directory creation and file writing\r\n\r\n### Integration Testing\r\n\r\n**Scope**: End-to-end testing of the complete change history extraction workflow\r\n\r\n**Key scenarios**:\r\n- Execute `ingest-csv` with change history configuration and verify CSV output\r\n- Test with various JQL queries (single ticket, multiple tickets, paginated results)\r\n- Test with tickets having different changelog structures (no changes, partial changes, complete history)\r\n- Verify that existing `ingest-csv` functionality (schedule calculation) continues to work correctly\r\n\r\n### End-to-End Testing\r\n\r\n**Scope**: Full workflow testing with real Jira instance\r\n\r\n**Key user journeys**:\r\n- Project manager configures JQL query and executes `ingest-csv` command\r\n- System extracts change history and generates CSV file in timestamped directory\r\n- Project manager opens CSV file and verifies data completeness and formatting\r\n- Verify that multiple executions create separate timestamped directories without overwriting\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Deployment Plan\r\n\r\n### Environments\r\n\r\n**Development**: Local development environment with test Jira instance for development and unit testing\r\n\r\n**Staging**: Staging environment with production-like Jira instance for integration testing\r\n\r\n**Production**: Production environment with live Jira instance for end users\r\n\r\n### Deployment Strategy\r\n\r\n**Approach**: Feature flag or configuration-based rollout - Change history extraction is enabled via configuration, allowing gradual rollout and easy disable if issues arise.\r\n\r\n**Rollback plan**: Remove or comment out change history configuration section to disable feature without code changes.\r\n\r\n**Monitoring**: Monitor command execution time, API call success rates, and CSV file generation success rates. Alert on errors or significant performance degradation.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Documentation Requirements\r\n\r\n**API Documentation**: Document new configuration options in configuration file schema documentation\r\n\r\n**User Documentation**: Update `ingest-csv` command documentation with change history extraction feature, configuration examples, and CSV output format description\r\n\r\n**Technical Documentation**: Document changelog data extraction approach (dmtools vs REST API), field mapping strategy, and error handling approach\r\n\r\n**Runbooks**: Document troubleshooting steps for common issues (API rate limiting, field mapping errors, file system permissions)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Timeline & Milestones\r\n\r\n**Milestone 1**: Configuration Extension and JQL Query Execution - Week 1\r\n\r\n**Milestone 2**: Changelog Data Extraction and Field Filtering - Week 2\r\n\r\n**Milestone 3**: Data Transformation, CSV Generation, and Integration - Week 2-3\r\n\r\n**Milestone 4**: Testing, Documentation, and Deployment - Week 3-4\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Open Questions\r\n\r\n**Question 1**: Should change history extraction be optional (config-driven) or always run? - **Owner**: Product Owner - **Status**: Resolved - Always run when configuration is provided\r\n\r\n**Question 2**: What is the maximum number of tickets that should be processed in a single run? - **Owner**: Technical Lead - **Status**: Open - To be determined during implementation based on performance testing\r\n\r\n**Question 3**: Should the system support filtering change history by date range? - **Owner**: Product Owner - **Status**: Resolved - Extract all history (no date filtering)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Appendix\r\n\r\n### References\r\n\r\n**[Reference 1]**: [MCP Tools Reference](https://github.com/kidblendapp/autocoding/blob/main/.dmtools/mcp-tools.md) - Documentation for dmtools commands including Jira API interactions\r\n\r\n**[Reference 2]**: [Jira REST API Changelog Documentation](https://developer.atlassian.com/cloud/jira/platform/rest/v3/api-group-issues/#api-rest-api-3-issue-issueidorkey-get) - Reference for changelog endpoint with expand parameter\r\n\r\n### Glossary\r\n\r\n**JQL**: Jira Query Language - Used to search and filter tickets in Jira\r\n\r\n**Changelog**: Historical record of all field changes made to a Jira ticket\r\n\r\n**Custom Field Code**: Internal identifier for custom fields in Jira (e.g., `customfield_10020` for Story Points)\r\n\r\n**ISO 8601**: International standard for date and time representation (format: `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss.sssZ`)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Story AC Coverage\r\n\r\n### Functional Criteria Coverage\r\n\r\n- **AC1** (JQL query execution): Covered by Task 1.2 - JQL Query Execution and Ticket Retrieval\r\n- **AC2** (Extract all changes for three fields): Covered by Task 1.3 - Changelog Data Extraction\r\n- **AC3** (CSV file creation in timestamped directory): Covered by Task 1.4 - Data Transformation and CSV Generation\r\n- **AC4** (CSV contains required columns): Covered by Task 1.4 - Data Transformation and CSV Generation\r\n- **AC5** (ISO 8601 timestamp format): Covered by Task 1.4 - Data Transformation and CSV Generation\r\n- **AC6** (Display names for users): Covered by Task 1.4 - Data Transformation and CSV Generation\r\n- **AC7** (Field mapping for custom fields): Covered by Task 1.3 - Changelog Data Extraction\r\n\r\n### Data Quality Criteria Coverage\r\n\r\n- **AC1** (Complete information in records): Covered by Task 1.3 and Task 1.4 - Changelog extraction and transformation ensure all required fields are present\r\n- **AC2** (Valid ISO 8601 timestamps): Covered by Task 1.4 - Data Transformation and CSV Generation\r\n- **AC3** (Correct user display names): Covered by Task 1.3 and Task 1.4 - Changelog extraction retrieves user information and transformation formats display names\r\n- **AC4** (Correct issue key association): Covered by Task 1.3 and Task 1.4 - Each changelog entry is associated with its ticket key during extraction and transformation\r\n\r\n### Integration Criteria Coverage\r\n\r\n- **AC1** (Runs as part of ingest-csv workflow): Covered by Task 1.5 - Integration with ingest-csv Command\r\n- **AC2** (Does not break existing functionality): Covered by Task 1.5 - Integration with ingest-csv Command\r\n- **AC3** (Error handling implemented): Covered by Task 1.3, Task 1.4, and Task 1.5 - Error handling is implemented at each stage","reporter":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/user?accountId=712020%3Aef0c8c11-3cf2-4fc0-97ac-2cdbf24d876c","accountId":"712020:ef0c8c11-3cf2-4fc0-97ac-2cdbf24d876c","avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d94c6869cf0cb2ecec022ada4bff7684?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Fdefault-avatar-2.png","24x24":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d94c6869cf0cb2ecec022ada4bff7684?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Fdefault-avatar-2.png","16x16":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d94c6869cf0cb2ecec022ada4bff7684?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Fdefault-avatar-2.png","32x32":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d94c6869cf0cb2ecec022ada4bff7684?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Fdefault-avatar-2.png"},"displayName":"KidBlend App ","active":true,"timeZone":"Europe/Minsk","accountType":"atlassian"},"fixVersions":[],"priority":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/priority/3","iconUrl":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/images/icons/priorities/medium_new.svg","name":"Medium","id":"3"},"labels":["ai_generated","ai_questions_asked"],"attachment":[],"issuelinks":[],"updated":"2025-12-17T06:49:29.369+0300","status":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/status/10069","description":"","iconUrl":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/","name":"IN REVIEW","id":"10069","statusCategory":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/statuscategory/4","id":4,"key":"indeterminate","colorName":"yellow","name":"In Progress"}}}}],"isLast":true}